rem Hexagonal Tile Differences
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=128
rem Find the Nth tile of a hexagonal
rem spiral with three prime differences
rem to its neighbours

use sequences
use io
use cli

arg Nth integer = 2000

rem Only the first and last tile of a
rem ring k can have three: their
rem neighbour differences are primes
rem 6k-1, 6k+1, 12k+5 and 6k-1, 6k+5,
rem 12k-7. Tiles 1 and 2 are special.
Top = Nth * 50
K = 2 to Top array
P1' = (6 * K - 1) in primes and (6 * K + 1) in primes and (12 * K + 5) in primes
P2' = (6 * K - 1) in primes and (6 * K + 5) in primes and (12 * K - 7) in primes
First' = 3 * K * (K - 1) + 2
Last' = 3 * K * (K + 1) + 1
Lo' = First filter P1 array
Hi' = Last filter P2 array
Hits' = (concat Lo Hi) sort
Tiles' = concat (array 1 2) Hits
Answer = Tiles (Nth - 1)
Answer print
